      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your feelings of shattered identity and the fear of being seen as a failure are incredibly heavy, but please remember that a person's inherent worth is not defined solely by their achievements or public perception. Recovery often involves a painful period of unlearning past labels to build a new sense of self that is more resilient than the old one; this process is uncomfortable, yet many people gradually find that respect returns not as expectation, but as genuine acceptance of their vulnerability. You are not your failures, and the shame you feel today is not a permanent stain on your character, even if it feels that way right now.",
